# headwear/helm/crested_crest: the crested helm's crest (P2c slice, SLICE-HELM-SHIELD): a horsehair brush in the plume slot
# (plumeColor; 0 = the tabard's colour) on a steel holder along the crown, front to back, its tail dropping behind the
# helm. Lit from the top-left: a lit cap row, a light front, the shadowed lower back. Height by the crest dial: crest1
# F-34 ... crest4 F-37 at rest (man; the woman a row lower); no dial = crest3. The bob lag (STYLE_P2 25.4, the delight):
# its own channel `crest` (proposed clip key: crest=up on every walk and run frame that names tuft=up, the head rising
# after the bob) draws the plume a row lower, so it follows the head a frame behind; every other frame draws rest (a
# swing's tuft=- never hides it). Written by the area's crestgen.py from hand-drawn crest4
# masters (each height keeps the drawn cap; checked by eye at every height). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body adult
role helm form9
role helm band5
layer headwear
anchor head
keys crest
z 1
tags overlay
legend Q plume 0
legend R plume 1
legend S plume 2
legend T plume 3
legend U plume 4
legend Z linen 4
legend k linen 3
legend l linen 2
legend D linen 1
legend I glow 4

view D key rest origin 0 4
|................
|.......QQ.......
|......QUTQ......
|......QTSQ......
|......QSRQ......
|......QSRQ......
|......vxwv......

# (LADDER-HEAD i2, w2/gen_top.py) the top of the ladder's crests, each with the bob lag (up: a row lower) and the
# stir (breeze): Mythic flame wings and a flame crest in the plume ramp; T6 white feathered wings swept up from the dome's
# sides (linen); T5 the great swept ostrich plume in the plume colour (D a fountain, the sides up over the crown and down
# (LADDER-HEAD i3, w3/gen_spire.py) Mythic D / U: the centre flame a phoenix spire standing 2 px proud of the side
# flames (their tops trimmed; C3b's plume ceiling unchanged)
# behind the neck guard). These win over the crest dial's views.
